+## Threads pin: v3.6.0 and the 3.1.0 to 3.6.0 contract audit (2026-11-26, hg-lnw.6)
+
+Graph pins official threads v3.6.0 `7c3c09082e8894ebceec9c060b769b07e359a2ad` (annotated tag `5bcb8a7b5f2ef0c1d0fd88b3b21870256e389852`), superseding v3.1.0. Wire `PROTOCOL_VERSION` stays 9 and `service_session_v1`..`v3` stay accepted. The node store is schema 19 (one-way: 3.3.0 moved it to 18, 3.5.0 to 19; 3.6.0 has no schema change). `Cargo.lock` resolves `herdr-threads` to 3.6.0 with no other dependency change. The graph library and binaries build against 3.6.0 with no source change (`cargo build`, `cargo build --all-features`). One test-only break: the fake service daemon in `src/threads/service_tests.rs` matches `ServiceOperation` exhaustively, and the enum has carried `ResurrectSeat` since 3.5.0, so it now answers that operation `Unsupported` like the other v3 lifecycle calls it does not model. At the pin commit the graph client still registered `service_session_v3`; hg-lnw.7 moved it to `service_session_v4` and calls `ResurrectSeat`. Daemon requirement once that lands: herdr-threads daemon ≥ 3.6.0. A daemon older than 3.5.0 refuses the v4 registration, and graph's registration-failure path reports it (no fallback to v3); 3.5.x serves v4, so graph's discovery refuses it by the descriptor's `software_version` (hg-lnw.25).
+
+Audit, from the herdr-threads CHANGELOG and source at each tag (3.1.0 to 3.5.0 from spec §2 of the hg-lnw design, at v3.5.0 `6aa914a`; 3.6.0 from `git log v3.5.0..v3.6.0` and the source at `7c3c090`). Graph's only threads CLI call is `thread list --seat` (`src/cli/adopt.rs`); every other call goes through the public service client.
+
+| Release | Change graph depends on | Graph action |
+|---|---|---|
