+| 3.1.2, 3.2.0, 3.2.1, 3.4.0, 3.4.1 | harness and text changes; `thread list --seat` unchanged | none |
+| 3.2.2 | person commands refused in an agent environment; operator repairs unaffected | none (graph runs no `human` command) |
+| 3.3.0 | node schema 18, one-way | daemon migration note |
+| 3.5.0 | node schema 19, one-way; every `Closed` retirement reversible, keyless included (7 d, obligations settle at 24 h); `service_session_v4` with `ResurrectSeat`; keyless `FinalizeRetirement` allowed (store-level, v3 too); new `RepairHistory.decision_kind` strings; test env `HT_TEST_OBLIGATION_EXPIRY_MS`, `HT_TEST_KEYLESS_FINALIZE_MS` (test-support builds) | keyless undo resurrects (spec §3, hg-lnw.4); daemon migration note; purge path keeps working |
+| 3.6.0, U1 (ht-lzhi) | `PersistentServiceClient::with_level(ServiceSessionLevel::V4)` registers `service_session_v4`; default stays V3; a daemon that does not serve the level refuses at register, no fallback. `submit` and replay refuse an operation above the client's level locally (`ServiceSessionLevel::required_by`: `ResurrectSeat` needs V4), before journaling, so the operation key is not consumed | the real adapter builds its client with `with_level(V4)` (hg-lnw.7) |
+| 3.6.0, U2 (ht-0f0r) | `ResurrectSeat { seat, target, host, replace, operation }` (v4, no new field) also restores a seat left unresolved and held by a Herdr restart, onto its own saved pane. New `ServiceResult::SeatAlreadyResolved(SeatId)` (wire `seat_already_resolved`) when a resumed session reattached first: nothing changed. Refusals: seat not reversible and not held on that pane, other pane, or a host kind that does not restore saved targets → `NotFound`; recovery reconciliation of the current host epoch not finished, or a kept continuity claim on the target → `ServiceBusy` (retry); `replace` set on a held seat → `InvalidRequest`. A hook whose continuity claim loses the race checks in onto the pane's owner | `rebind_held_seat` = `ResurrectSeat` with `replace: None` (spec §4); the adapter maps `SeatAlreadyResolved` to done and `ServiceBusy` to transient (hg-lnw.7). The adapter's `restore_outcome` matches `SeatAlreadyResolved` explicitly; no catch-all arm reads it |
+| 3.6.0, other | macOS Codex queue wake (ht-8t52), herdr-core 0.1.22 added to tested releases, macOS symlinked-path canonicalization; no store schema change; peer wire frozen | none |
+
+ResurrectSeat at 3.6.0 still carries ht-eu3v's semantics with the windows hg-lnw.2's fake models: `src/store/seats/reversible.rs` is unchanged since v3.5.0, with `OBLIGATION_EXPIRY_MS` = 24 h (pending ACK requests and ordinary invitations settle as recipient-retired) and `KEYLESS_FINALIZE_MS` = 7 d (the retirement becomes final), overridable in test-support builds through `TEST_OBLIGATION_EXPIRY_ENV` (`HT_TEST_OBLIGATION_EXPIRY_MS`) and `TEST_KEYLESS_FINALIZE_ENV` (`HT_TEST_KEYLESS_FINALIZE_MS`).
+
+Authority: in 3.6.0 both the resurrect and the restore case run `reversible::require_v4_authority`, which accepts a keyless seat (no continuity key) from any v4 service session and requires the key owner for a keyed seat (`src/store/seats/operator.rs` `service_case_of`, `src/store/seats/reversible.rs`). hg-lnw.7 checked it against the shipped code at `7c3c090`: in `mutate_operator_guarded` the service actor's `service_case_of` (resurrect, held-seat restore or already resolved) is followed by `require_v4_authority` for every case, and the check reads only the seat's current continuity key (`continuity_keys::key_of_seat`), not when or by whom the seat was adopted, so a keyless seat adopted before the upgrade qualifies from any v4 session.
+
+ResurrectSeat op-key idempotency (hg-lnw.7, same code): the daemon runs the decision in `execute_idempotent_transaction` under the service session's scope (`service:<instance>:<author>`) with a digest of the typed operator command (seat, target, host, replace, key). A success is stored and a replay under the key returns it; the same key with a changed payload (another `replace`, pane or seat) is refused `OperationPayloadMismatch`; a refusal rolls the transaction back and stores nothing, so a retry under the same key is a fresh decision. Graph's client intent journal keeps a definitive refusal as the key's completion, which `mutate` would replay once; the adapter forgets it after every restore refusal, so a `NotFound` or `StaleHostObservation` retried under the same key reaches the daemon again. `ServiceBusy` and a dropped call keep the intent pending and replay its original envelope. A changed payload needs a new key, which the resurrect executor's key (`resurrect:<clone>:<epoch>:<replace or none>:<refusal count>`) provides. The adapter maps the answers per the hg-lnw.14 split: `SeatResurrected` done, `SeatAlreadyResolved` already resolved (done), `ServiceBusy` (and `StoreBusy`), `StaleHostObservation`, transport trouble and an unknown outcome transient; `NotFound`, `Unauthorized`, `TargetAlreadyOwned`, `InvalidRequest` (also `OperationPayloadMismatch`), `Unsupported` (also a refused v4 registration) and `InstanceMismatch` definitive. Graph registers `with_level(ServiceSessionLevel::V4)`; a pre-3.5.0 daemon's `unsupported service capability` refusal is the named error `herdr-threads daemon refused service_session_v4 (...); upgrade the herdr-threads daemon to >= 3.6.0`, shown by the `threads` status component and the doctor's `threads` check with the upgrade step.
